From 14b53b5883288480a42d358f95c3bb48104549aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(cuda): a launch with no captured Triton variant runs
 the closest more general one

Before: a prompt whose length gives a kernel argument a specialization class that no recording captured
stopped on MissingTritonVariant, a 500 where the served lane answers. One example is 2,064 tokens:
_index_score's n is a multiple of 16 but its tile count, 33, is not.

After: Set.find falls back to the fitting variant that assumes the least less. It must have the same
constexprs, and every assumption it was compiled with must hold for the launch: an argument it takes as
16-divisible is 16-divisible, and an int it folded to 1 is 1. Triton's specializations change which loads
vectorize and which masks fold, not the arithmetic, so the bits are the same. The first fallback of each
variant is named on stderr. TF_AOT_WEAKEST=1 runs every launch on its most general fitting variant, to gate
that claim.

Gate (two GB10 nodes, build pg26 = this commit):
- With TF_AOT_WEAKEST=1 (55 to 88 variants a run swapped for more general ones), every text gate is
  equal: v26w 3663, v26l 10655, v26s 9025, v26r 2107, v26k 1024 and v26L 64 on both ranks, and lane gates
  12/12, 7/7, 1/1.
- Also with TF_AOT_WEAKEST=1, the server: vision gate 6/6, visionref 9/9 and 18/18 at four at once, 51 of
  51 probes equal to the lane, gates.py PASS, concurrent == solo 12/12.
- As served, the 51 probes are equal to the lane. The 2,064-token prompt is the one fallback
  (_index_score).
